{
 "sentence": "To check that this is not in-sample fitting, we refit the slope on training folds only and evaluate it on held-out ones: leaving one experiment family out (12 folds) gives an out-of-sample $R^2$ of $0.449$ pooled and $0.396$ at the median fold, with $67\\%$ of folds beating the training-fold constant baseline; leaving one dataset$\\times$model cell out (6 folds) gives $0.236$ and $0.227$, with $67\\%$ of folds beating it. The association therefore transfers, but not uniformly: in both schemes the weakest fold is SigLIP, where the ordering is known to reverse, which is why we report an association with its per-fold spread rather than a predictive relation.",
